GPT-6.2 Sol (Codex's default) and GPT-6.2 Astra now send tool calls through OpenAI's Responses API instead of Chat Completions, so tools work with them again. Full gate is green: fmt, clippy with -D warnings, and cargo test (48 suites, 7695 passed, 0 failed). The working tree is clean.

The change is in commit 2da2af4a (Part of #1060). In the openai provider branch, any gpt-6* id without a yoagent preset is now built from yoagent's ModelConfig::generic("openai", id), and yoagent's own code picks Responses. I didn't copy that logic into yoyo, and the base-URL handling is unchanged.

First request each id sent to a local stub on 127.0.0.1 (no real OpenAI host), tools on:

| id | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| gpt-6-sol, gpt-6.1-sol | /responses | /responses |
| gpt-6.2-sol, gpt-6.2-astra | /chat/completions | /responses |
| gpt-6.3-sol (made up) | /chat/completions | /responses |
| gpt-5.5, o3, gpt-4o | /chat/completions | /chat/completions |

The made-up gpt-6.3-sol row means the next GPT-6 release won't need a list edit. gpt-5.x and the o-series are deliberately unchanged: I didn't check OpenAI's docs for those families, so row 1 of #1060 stays open.

A problem I found and fixed in the same commit: the "no preset known, using guessed limits" warning compares a model's limits with Chat Completions defaults. After this change, models without a preset get the Responses defaults (128000 / 16000), so the warning would have gone quiet for exactly the models now running on guessed limits. I added a second comparison against made-up gpt-6 ids, and the built binary now prints the warning for gpt-6.2-sol. The real GPT-6.2 limits aren't wired in because yoagent 0.27.9 has no GPT-6.2 preset.

Two tests expected the old Chat Completions route for gpt-6 ids. I changed them rather than deleting them:
• near_misses_keep_the_bare_openai_config still checks these ids don't match a preset (the misbilling guard), but now expects Responses.
• The guessed-limits wording test now uses gpt-5.9-test, and a new test checks gpt-6 ids against yoagent's own Responses defaults.

Other changes:
• gpt-6.2-sol and gpt-6.2-astra are on the known openai models list, so the "Unknown model" warning no longer fires for them. They're also offered in /model completion, with gpt-6-sol and gpt-6.1-sol. The 6.2 ids come from OpenAI's GPT-6.2 guide, cited in the code.
• models.md says gpt-6 ids use Responses, and that a --base-url proxy serving only /chat/completions should use --provider custom.
• tests/module_size.rs has new line counts for agent_builder.rs and commands.rs.

Checks: I broke each fix on purpose and confirmed the tests catch it. Disabling the new route made 3 tests fail by name, and disabling the warning fix made 4 fail. Both were restored, with the marker count back to 0. The before table, after table and both results are posted on #1060 (three comments) and in the commit body.

One related check: at default thinking, gpt-6.2-sol's request carries no reasoning field, so yoyo doesn't send the none effort OpenAI says 6.2 rejects. I didn't test the other --thinking levels. Rows 1, 2 and 4 of #1060 remain open.

